WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.695 --> 00:00:02.420
- [Narrator] See Paige.

00:00:02.420 --> 00:00:03.931
See Paige play.

00:00:03.931 --> 00:00:05.279
Play, Paige, pl--

00:00:05.279 --> 00:00:07.862
What the hell is Paige playing?

00:00:13.365 --> 00:00:16.978
This is an orchestra
comprised entirely of flutes.

00:00:16.978 --> 00:00:20.319
This works because flutes
can cover the entire range

00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:22.608
of an orchestra on their own,

00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:24.761
from the piccolo at the
top (piccolo whistles),

00:00:24.761 --> 00:00:26.457
all the way to the double contrabass flute

00:00:26.457 --> 00:00:28.938
down at the bottom (double
contrabass flute booms).

00:00:28.938 --> 00:00:30.553
Very cool.

00:00:30.553 --> 00:00:33.568
And there's Paige playing,
you know, back from the intro.

00:00:33.568 --> 00:00:36.461
- I'm Paige Long, and I'm
a professional flutist.

00:00:36.461 --> 00:00:39.565
- [Narrator] Wait, flutist or flautist?

00:00:39.565 --> 00:00:40.689
- I like flutist.

00:00:40.689 --> 00:00:42.500
- [Narrator] She's one of
a handful of people playing

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:45.531
the three largest flutes
in the flute family:

00:00:45.531 --> 00:00:48.617
the contrabass flute,
the subcontrabass flute,

00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:51.492
and the double contrabass flute.

00:00:51.492 --> 00:00:54.094
Let's learn about big flutes.

00:00:54.094 --> 00:00:56.593
- [Paige] In its case, the
double contrabass flute weighs

00:00:56.593 --> 00:00:58.431
approximately 30 pounds.

00:00:58.431 --> 00:01:02.598
It stands over eight feet tall,
and it's 22 feet of tubing.

00:01:03.921 --> 00:01:08.088
The subcontrabass flute in
G has 11 feet of tubing,

00:01:08.516 --> 00:01:12.266
and the contrabass in
C has 9 feet of tubing.

00:01:13.142 --> 00:01:15.246
- [Narrator] So, how does
one play an instrument

00:01:15.246 --> 00:01:17.412
with 22 feet of tubing?

00:01:17.412 --> 00:01:18.845
- [Paige] For these lower flutes,

00:01:18.845 --> 00:01:20.217
it's a whole different technique.

00:01:20.217 --> 00:01:21.928
Your embouchure is looser--

00:01:21.928 --> 00:01:23.462
- [Narrator] New word!

00:01:23.462 --> 00:01:24.766
Embouchure.

00:01:24.766 --> 00:01:25.849
Em-bou-chure.

00:01:26.947 --> 00:01:28.316
Embouchure.

00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:30.129
- [Paige] Embouchure is the
way you shape your mouth

00:01:30.129 --> 00:01:33.266
to make a sound on the flute.

00:01:33.266 --> 00:01:37.433
Your mouth is looser,
bigger, takes a lot more air,

00:01:38.246 --> 00:01:40.236
and a lot more support.

00:01:40.236 --> 00:01:43.642
I feel like I've run a 10k
when I'm done with a concert.

00:01:43.642 --> 00:01:46.510
- [Narrator] 'Cause it's hard
to get a clean, low sound?

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:48.363
- [Paige] They actually play
the lowest possible notes

00:01:48.363 --> 00:01:50.750
of an orchestral instrument.

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.114
- [Narrator] Say, lowest of
any orchestral instrument?

00:01:54.114 --> 00:01:55.585
Now what does that mean?

00:01:55.585 --> 00:01:57.812
Hey, guys, can you help us out here?

00:01:57.812 --> 00:01:59.186
- [Man] Well, alright.

00:01:59.186 --> 00:02:00.019
Ready, boys?

00:02:00.019 --> 00:02:02.660
♪ The double contrabass flute goes low ♪

00:02:02.660 --> 00:02:05.069
♪ Lower than any instrument can go ♪

00:02:05.069 --> 00:02:06.952
♪ Lower than the string
bass, that big old guy ♪

00:02:06.952 --> 00:02:10.270
♪ He makes that bass line fly ♪

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:11.812
- [Narrator] And what's next?

00:02:11.812 --> 00:02:13.908
- [Man] It's the subcontrabass flute!

00:02:13.908 --> 00:02:15.266
Hit it!

00:02:15.266 --> 00:02:17.474
♪ Another big flute
sounds like a bassoon ♪

00:02:17.474 --> 00:02:19.732
♪ The subcontrabass can carry a tune ♪

00:02:19.732 --> 00:02:21.981
♪ The contrabass flute
is the smallest fellow ♪

00:02:21.981 --> 00:02:25.305
♪ It sounds just like a cello ♪

00:02:25.305 --> 00:02:26.622
- [Narrator] Wow, thanks!

00:02:26.622 --> 00:02:28.591
Now I understand.

00:02:28.591 --> 00:02:31.679
So Paige, what do you like
about these giant flutes?

00:02:31.679 --> 00:02:34.626
- [Paige] In the land of flutes,
they're like the subculture

00:02:34.626 --> 00:02:36.123
of the flute community.

00:02:36.123 --> 00:02:39.738
And we provide a role that
the concert flute cannot.

00:02:39.738 --> 00:02:41.070
- [Narrator] It all checks out.

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:42.839
Paige, play us out.

00:02:42.839 --> 00:02:45.756
(flute trio plays)

